# What `cargo xtask build` packs into BOOTFS.IMG (docs/10 section 5.2).
# path | source | name | display name | class | mem_mib | flags
# source is program:<binary> or file:<path from the workspace root>;
# class is app or system; mem_mib 0 is the default limit; flags is - or a
# comma-separated list of critical, display and corrupt:wx. corrupt:wx is
# for the build: the entry gets the program with a segment made writable
# and executable, an image the kernel must refuse to start.
